# Build a Blackguard and photograph two things bd inc-tek.8.3 changed about
# him: his weapon and armour proficiencies (PA-03-F11) and the creature his
# Fiendish Servant summons (PA-03-F15).
#
# PA-03-F11. The class prose promised "blades, impact weapons, polearms and
# spears, and with all classes of armour" and the class declared no
# Proficiencies: field at all, so it granted none of them. Shields were added
# to the prose and the grant together, on Brian's ruling, which also brings
# Incursion into line with the SRD blackguard. The field is now
#   Proficiencies: WG_SBLADES, WG_LBLADES, WG_IMPACT, WG_POLEARMS,
#                  WG_SPEARS, WG_LARMOUR, WG_MARMOUR, WG_HARMOUR, WG_SHIELDS;
# and the sheet's Proficiencies line (src/Sheet.cpp:861-876) reports it.
#
# PA-03-F15 is NOT tested here, and the reason is a hard limit rather than a
# choice. The Fiendish Servant arrives at Blackguard 5, and this character
# cannot get there. MAX_CHAR_LEVEL is 11 (inc/Defines.h:4367) and
# src/Create.cpp:2210 enforces it, so the eight core levels this gate costs
# leave room for three. Entering with fewer core levels is not possible
# either: the gate wants a base attack bonus of +6, which only a class
# attacking at 100% reaches inside six levels, and no such class carries
# Knowledge (Infernal). See tools/keys/fiendish-servant.keys, which reaches
# the same effect by another road.
#
# THE BUILD. The gate wants an Evil alignment, Intimidate 12, Knowledge
# (Infernal) 10 and a base attack bonus of +6 in some category
# (lib/prestige.irh:687-712). A rogue carries both skills -- SK_KNOW_ALL in
# its skill list expands to every Knowledge id, including SK_KNOW_INF
# (inc/Defines.h:1888) -- and reaches melee BAB +6 at 8th level. So: Rogue 8.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral Evil"  # the class refuses anyone who is not Evil
@choose "Alertness"
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a          # however many feats are asked for

# Eighteen ranks, two to a skill. The two the gate reads first; the rest only
# because character generation will not release a character with a rank
# unspent.
@cursorto:mark "Intimidate" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Infern" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Athletics" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Balance" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Climb" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Craft" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                               # character sheet
@until "Class  Rogue 8" G       # eight core levels, for BAB +6

S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Intimidate" DOWN
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Knowledge (Infern" DOWN
RIGHT*10
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Blackguard"
@expect "Blackguard 0"          # the gate let him in

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Blackguard"
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Blackguard"
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Blackguard"
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
@while "Air':?" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@expect "Blackguard 3"

W                       # Write Dump
b g u a r d ENTER       # filename: "bguard"
ESC
@quit
